#Lua SEXPs

$Operator: is-campaign?
$Category: Status
$Subcategory: LUA-Condition
$Minimum Arguments: 0
$Maximum Arguments: 0
$Return Type: Boolean
$Description: This sexp checks to see if the current mission is being played in a campaign or the Tech-room. Returns true if in a campaign and false if not.

$Operator: difficulty-number
$Category: Status
$Subcategory: LUA-Condition
$Minimum Arguments: 0
$Maximum Arguments: 0
$Return Type: Number
$Description: This sexp returns the difficulty level from 1-5, 1 being the lowest, (Beginner) and 5 being the highest (Elite).

$Operator: variable-divide
$Category: Status
$Subcategory: LUA-Condition
$Minimum Arguments: 2
$Maximum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Number
$Description: Divides two number variables and returns the percent rounded to the closest whole number. In other words, the SEXP returns (var1.Value/var2.Value)*100.   
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Variable 1, the numerator. The variable needs to be a number. 
	+Type: Variable	
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Variable 2, the denominator. The variable needs to be a number. 
	+Type: Variable	

$Operator: number-to-time
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 2
$Maximum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp takes a number and converts it to a time format saves it to a string variable (IE input of 90 becomes 1:30). 
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Number to convert to string format. 
	+Type: Number
$Parameter: 
	+Description: String variable to save value to. 
	+Type: Variable

