$Operator: set-player-target-sub
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 1
$Maximum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp sets the player's target to a specific ship and subsystem. Does not work in multiplayer.
$Parameter: 	
	+Description: Ship to set as target.
	+Type: Ship
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Subsystem to set as target.
	+Type: Subsystem

$Operator: set-shield-recharge-percent
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp sets the shield recharge percent rate of a given ship.
$Parameter: 	
	+Description: New shield recharge percent value. Value of 100 is 100% recharge per second. Value of 1 is 1% recharge per second. Values less then 0 will be set to 0. Note, this sexp only works in singelplayer.
	+Type: Number
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Ship(s) to set.
	+Type: Ship

$Operator: set-shield-special-hitpoints
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp sets a given ship's shields with special hitpoints by changing the maximum and remaining hitpoints. Useful to make individual ship's shields weaker or stronger. Note, this sexp only works in singelplayer. 
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Percentage to use to calculate the new special shield hitpoints. For example, to make a shield twice as strong, set this to 200. Must be greater than 0. 
	+Type: Number
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Ship(s) on which the special shield hitpoints will be set. Must be in the mission. 
	+Type: Ship

$Operator: set-hull-special-hitpoints
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp sets a given ship's hull with special hitpoints by changing the maximum and remaining hitpoints. Useful to make individual ship's hull weaker or stronger. Note, this sexp only works in singelplayer. 
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Percentage to use to calculate the new special hull hitpoints. For example, to make a hull twice as strong, set this to 200. Must be greater than 0. 
	+Type: Number
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Ship(s) on which the special hull hitpoints will be set. Must be in the mission. 
	+Type: Ship

$Operator: set-subsystem-special-hitpoints
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 3
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp sets a given subsystem with special hitpoints by changing the maximum and remaining hitpoints. Useful to make individual subsystems weaker or stronger. Note, this sexp only works in singelplayer. 
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Percentage to use to calculate the new special hitpoints. For example, to make a subsystem twice as strong, set this to 200. Must be greater than 0. 
	+Type: Number
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Ship on which the subystem special hitpoints will be set. Must be in the mission. 
	+Type: Ship
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Subsystems to set.
	+Type: Subsystem

$Operator: set-impact-armor-type
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 2
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp sets the Impact Armor type of a given ship to either Low Damage Impact Armor or High Damage Impact Armor.
$Parameter: 	
	+Description: The type of Impact Armor to set, where 0 is the default Low Damage Impact Armor and 1 is the High Damage Impact Armor. Values less then 0 will be set to 0. Note, this sexp only works in singelplayer.
	+Type: Number
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Ship(s) to set.
	+Type: Ship

$Operator: set-guarders-to-orbit
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 1
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: This sexp tells any craft guarding this ship to orbit the ship when guarding, even if it is a small ship. Does nothing to ships that have a radius of >= 50 meters, since the AI already always orbits those ships. Note, this sexp only works in singelplayer.
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Ship(s) to set.
	+Type: Ship

#End